{"author":{"id":"686d9350e5e426946f54ca7a73ceeef9fd8682b44ea6617ce58187e451c43768"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790960716,"nonce":"CaBxY3MUXENj5AuWGtXESWXGcyE=","title":"replace the test-only hlwindow with an adapter over xwindow","message":"crates/hlwindow is a winit binding kept for tests and not shipped, so Ash and HashLink programs have no window library to give xgpu a surface. xwindow (github.com/rayzor-blade/xwindow) generates the `window` API for HashLink from the declaration Caribou and Rayzor use, over winit natively and the page's canvas in a browser. An adapter over it, shipped as `xwindow.hdll` (and `xwindow.wasm` for Ash in a page), replaces hlwindow and serves the tests.\n\nA scratch adapter built from hlwgpu's runtime module already runs under Ash: it opens a window, reports platform, size, scale and monitor, polls events as Haxe enums (nested ones included) and passes them to `GpuInstance.surface(window.platform(), window.raw(0..3))`'s table. It needs the Buffer layout change in hlwgpu's runtime (the issue on Buffer layout) and `xwindow_bindgen::generate(Runtime::HashLink)` with `xwindow_backend::install`; the Haxe tree comes from `xwindow-haxe ash`.","files":null}]}